  "next_action": "Merge the PR for claude/m3-slice3b (TASK-20261123-004). Then M3 slice 3c under a model-class task: availability and role features (snap, target, air-yard, carry and red-zone shares; injury and practice status through arbit_model.availability; teammates' absences), with weather W1 beside it. Ask the owner for the NWS User-Agent contact before W3.",
  "sections": {
    "review": {
      "summary": "Read ADR-006's team-first structure and the methods research: team environment and opponent first, D/ST mostly the opponent, constants as games for half signal. Read the signal study's team definitions (stats_team: plays = attempts + sacks + carries, dropbacks = attempts + sacks, EPA = passing + rushing; sacks forced and takeaways from the opponent row) and its split_half method; the targets module (per-game SeasonRows, athlete and defense lines); and the stat-line adapter's play and team columns. The stored slice 2 targets (index 4afbd836) cover 2012-2026 through 2026-11-10. No measured constant existed for FFA points allowed by position.",
      "files": [
        "docs/architecture/decisions/006-model-architecture.md",
        "docs/research/ffa-projection-methods-2026-11-09.md",
        "docs/research/ffa-signal-study-2026-11-09.json",
        "scripts/model/ffa_signal_study.py",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/targets.py",
        "libs/arbit-data/src/arbit_data/nflverse/stat_lines.py"
      ]
    },
    "plan": {
      "summary": "Add _manifest to readings; gamebook.py scoring each completed game known at the decision with the shared scorer, cached per version combination; a study measuring split-half constants for FFA points allowed by position and D/ST points allowed (raw and adjusted for offenses faced) with the signal study's method; feature_specs.py with definition, unit, window, cutoff, sources and constants for every column; team_features.py producing team rates (raw, shrunk, last season), opponent defense, defense against the position and context per team per game; tests including a mutation test and constants-versus-receipt; a read-only real-data audit; docs.",
      "files": [
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/gamebook.py",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/team_features.py",
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/feature_specs.py",
        "scripts/model/defense_position_study.py"
      ]
    },
    "implementation": {
      "summary": "point_in_time: readings carry _manifest. gamebook.py: Gamebooks.at(season, at) reads schedules (scores), pbp, player and team statistics through the reader, keeps games with all four known, scores each with targets() once per version combination, and returns team-games (signal study definitions), FFA points and opportunities by position, and D/ST points. defense_position_study.py: stability of points allowed by position and D/ST points allowed, raw and leave-one-out adjusted, 2016-2025, receipt committed. feature_specs.py: 65 specs and 20 constants with receipt paths. team_features.py: features per team per game, grouped by decision time, with coverage and lineage. team_features_audit.py and receipt. Docs: research note, ENG-056, README, plan, status, changelog.",
      "files": [
        "libs/arbit-model/src/arbit_model/point_in_time.py",
